{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261110T172025Z-82e93fdb", "ts": "2026-11-10T17:22:55Z", "actor": {"worktree": "arrt-player", "plugin": "3.8.1-dev", "branch": "feature/settings-ui", "build": "52bb14851a37"}, "body": {"base_commit": "9b42f47c9c208e73ac91cc5c2f0aab3c3e233491", "base_tree": "269f50d5157163532ea97d662c0fb107778d5179", "head_tree": "c32d7b1987e724da2526b6b66b5deb1cda08e3f7", "head_commit": "44eb9b0673b61c525747accbe17f38a5788143d5", "dispatch_commit": "44eb9b0673b61c525747accbe17f38a5788143d5", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args chunk redirected: working tree is clean, so chunk/final would dispatch an empty interval; branch is 1 commit(s) ahead of origin/develop and no cumulative record covers current HEAD \u2014 the committed bundle is cumulative's scope", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": [".env.example", "src/arrt_player/__main__.py", "src/arrt_player/config.py", "src/arrt_player/settings_ui/__init__.py", "src/arrt_player/settings_ui/auth.py", "src/arrt_player/settings_ui/server.py", "src/arrt_player/settings_ui/store.py", "tests/test_client.py", "tests/test_config.py", "tests/test_plane_isolation.py", "tests/test_settings_ui.py"], "files_changed": [".env.example", ".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-settings-ui.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/nonfunctional-requirements.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/security-model.md", ".prawduct/changes/settings-ui.md", "src/arrt_player/__main__.py", "src/arrt_player/config.py", "src/arrt_player/settings_ui/__init__.py", "src/arrt_player/settings_ui/auth.py", "src/arrt_player/settings_ui/server.py", "src/arrt_player/settings_ui/store.py", "tests/test_client.py", "tests/test_config.py", "tests/test_plane_isolation.py", "tests/test_settings_ui.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-settings-ui.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/nonfunctional-requirements.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/security-model.md", ".prawduct/changes/settings-ui.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "blocking", "title": "Referrer-Policy: no-referrer makes every real browser send `Origin: null` on the page's own form POSTs, which _same_origin_posts refuses, so setup, login and logout cannot work from a browser", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why it broke: the Fetch standard ('append a request Origin header') sets the serialized origin to `null` for a non-GET, non-CORS request (a form submission) whenever the request's referrer policy is `no-referrer`, and the form inherits the document's policy from SECURITY_HEADERS (server.py:56); `_same_origin_posts` (server.py:142) then compares `null` with `http://host:port` and returns 403, and test_settings_ui.py's TestWhatThePageRefuses asserts exactly that `Origin: null` is refused. Every test POST passes only because the `post()` helper hand-sets a correct Origin, which a browser under this policy never sends ('When a double stands in for a stateful client, fail where the real one fails'). So the chunk's acceptance criterion ('The page accepts the code, sets a password, logs in and out') fails in practice, and the plan's Verification Strategy browser run on the Mac has no recorded evidence. Fix: change the policy to `same-origin` (same-origin POSTs keep their Origin; nothing, including the setup code in the query, is sent cross-origin) and update the security-model bullet that lists `no-referrer`; pin it with a test that asserts the Referrer-Policy is one under which a same-origin form POST keeps its Origin (not a self-referential equality against SECURITY_HEADERS), and run the plan's browser check once and record it.", "files": ["src/arrt_player/settings_ui/server.py", "tests/test_settings_ui.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "The settings page's guard exempts `import aiohttp.web`, which binds `aiohttp` and leaves `aiohttp.request(...)` reachable, though the docstring, architecture.md and the commit say the page may spell it `from aiohttp.web import` and no other way", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why: `_exempt` (test_plane_isolation.py) accepts any offence whose name is `aiohttp.web`, and `imported_names` yields that name for a plain `import aiohttp.web` too, so the spelling rule is not what the guard checks; the planted case `import aiohttp.web; aiohttp.ClientSession()` is caught only by CLIENT_NAMES, and CLIENT_NAMES lacks `request`, aiohttp's top-level client function. A future edit to server.py could open an outbound request with the guard green. 'When you write or cite 'exactly one', 'always' or 'never', state what the store or guard actually enforces.' Fix by enforcing the stated spelling (refuse an `ast.Import` of aiohttp.* in the page module) and add a planted `import aiohttp.web\\naiohttp.request(...)` case that must fail.", "files": ["tests/test_plane_isolation.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "The login throttle checks before `await request.post()` and records the failure after it, so concurrent attempts all pass one window; and each attempt runs scrypt synchronously on the event loop the walls share", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why: `_login` (server.py:220-226) reads `wait_seconds()` and only calls `failed()` after awaiting the body, so an unauthenticated LAN client that sends N requests' headers and then their bodies together gets N guesses per throttle window; each guess is a blocking hashlib.scrypt (n=2^14, r=8, ~16 MiB, tenths of a second on a Pi 4 per auth.py's own comment) on the loop that runs the supervisor, the pulls and the Frame's websocket, which architecture.md otherwise keeps off the loop ('blocking, on a thread'). security-model.md's Abuse Prevention row claims guessing is bounded by 'a throttle doubling to a minute per attempt', which holds only for serial attempts. Fix: read the form first, then check-and-reserve the attempt synchronously (no await between the throttle check and recording the attempt), and run the scrypt off the loop (asyncio.to_thread) only after the reservation; add a test that fires two concurrent wrong-password POSTs and asserts the second is 429.", "files": ["src/arrt_player/settings_ui/server.py", "src/arrt_player/settings_ui/auth.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "record-lint change-fragment: .prawduct/changes/settings-ui.md has an empty narrative and an empty consumer note", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Machine-answered (record_lint change-fragment x2): the fragment carries only its frontmatter and an empty `## Consumer note`. The plan assigns the narrative and note to chunk 03; until then a PR cut from this branch ships a change record that says nothing. Write the narrative above the consumer note and the note itself (or `none: <reason>`).", "files": [".prawduct/changes/settings-ui.md"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "setup_url and home_url do not bracket an IPv6 UI_BIND", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `address_to_visit` returns a literal UI_BIND such as `::1` or `fd00::5` unchanged, and `setup_url` formats `http://::1:8771/...`, which no browser parses. Only matters if the operator sets an IPv6 UI_BIND; bracket an address containing ':' or refuse IPv6 in load_ui.", "files": ["src/arrt_player/settings_ui/server.py"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions and goals, for the owner", "recommendation": "Scope: none. The plan's 'Decisions made mid-build' section is empty; the vetoable DECISIONs (the narrowed plane-isolation guard, the setup code as the one logged credential) and the owner-proposed NFR \u00a7 Start-up amendment are recorded with dispositions for every governing artifact. Inferred items still open to veto: environment-wins precedence, port 8771 and 0.0.0.0 default, 30-day cookie, Origin check plus SameSite=Strict, hand-edit password recovery. Goals Level is Medium-High with the stated raiser met by test_without_a_server_the_player_serves_only_its_page_and_says_where. Backlog reconciliation: none of the 23 open items is resolved by this change; the Goals' claim that 'a backlog item records' wave 2 names no item and none is open yet.", "fid": "R-6"}], "counts": {"blocking": 1, "warning": 3, "note": 2}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 720, "scope": "settings-ui", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["01"], "chunks_proposed": ["01"], "chunk": "01", "base_reviewed": "9b42f47c9c208e73ac91cc5c2f0aab3c3e233491", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-settings-ui.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/nonfunctional-requirements.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/security-model.md", ".prawduct/changes/settings-ui.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-settings-ui.md", "findings": [{"check": "change-fragment", "path": ".prawduct/changes/settings-ui.md", "line": null, "detail": "empty-narrative: say what changed and why above the consumer note"}, {"check": "change-fragment", "path": ".prawduct/changes/settings-ui.md", "line": null, "detail": "empty-consumer-note: write the note, or `none: <reason>` when there is nothing to tell consumers"}], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 2, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-10T17:20:25Z"}}

